{
  "schema": 1,
  "title": "Digimon Venom NXT crowded-world client performance benchmark",
  "environment": {
    "platform": "Linux-6.18.44-x86_64-with-glibc2.39",
    "python": "3.12.14",
    "pygame_ce": "2.5.8",
    "video_driver": "dummy",
    "audio_driver": "dummy"
  },
  "methodology": [
    "Sequential baseline/fixed processes with no concurrent tests or packaging; 960 warmup frames then 360 measured frames per run. The primary 160-rival case has three paired repeats; other scenarios have one pair.",
    "Actual App.update, WorldRenderer.update and App.draw paths, including native UI, background, map, sprites, shadows, nameplates, minimap, snapshot ingestion and interpolation. No FPS limiter; SDL dummy display and dummy audio.",
    "Physical framebuffer 2048x1152, native UI scale 4/3, original x2 Dawn Sector 004 map and original animation assets, zoom1.5. No resolution reduction, sprite reduction, or bot-count reduction.",
    "All 64 tamer appearances (or bot count if smaller), up to128 distinct lead species selected deterministically from the1004-species catalog, one partner per rival, plus the local tamer and partner. Crowds seeded with4096.",
    "Synthetic snapshots arrive every6 simulated frames (10Hz), animation/interpolation advances at fixed60Hz for equal work regardless of actual benchmark speed. Directions cycle through eight poses over16 simulated seconds; warmup covers that cycle.",
    "Panning moves the local camera through a repeatable sinusoidal path while rivals continue moving. Synthetic snapshot construction is excluded from timed blocks; incoming JSON parsing belongs to the real transport thread and is also excluded.",
    "A fresh temporary settings file isolates each run from player preferences. PNG load calls are counted with the same lightweight wrapper in both versions. All runs reported zero asset errors.",
    "Measured times describe Linux headless CPU frame preparation, not Windows display FPS, GPU presentation, live network latency, database/server simulation cost, or a promise for a specific PC. Cold first-visit loading is excluded by warmup.",
    "Primary summaries use the median of three per-run means and separately the median of three per-run percentiles. They are not pooled frame-time percentiles."
  ],
  "initial_profile": {
    "scope": "Separate diagnostic profile,160 rivals,360 warmup frames,180 profiled frames; excluded from unprofiled timing summary.",
    "png_decodes": 4510,
    "pygame_image_load_cumulative_seconds": 4.023,
    "assets_image_cumulative_seconds": 4.866,
    "profile_total_seconds": 11.107,
    "finding": "Small cache-entry caps repeatedly evicted active animation frames; image loads and decoding continued after warmup. Client/network update was a small share of frame time."
  },
  "visual_check": "Baseline and fixed primary screenshots were inspected. Native UI and actors remain present and sharp. Frame hashes differ because bounded map blocks use a different nearest-neighbor sampling phase; the difference image showed map-edge sampling changes without added smoothing.",
  "reproduce": [
    "python -m tools.benchmark_client_fps --bots 160 --warmup 960 --frames 360 --json fixed.json",
    "python tools/benchmark_client_fps.py --project /path/to/original/DigimonVenomNXT --bots 160 --warmup 960 --frames 360 --json baseline.json",
    "Add --pan for the panning case; use --bots 20 or --bots 256 for the other cases. Repeat the primary pair three times, sequentially."
  ],
